cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FALCON: Enterprise Cryptographic Discovery and Post-Quantum Migration Intelligence"
message: "If you use FALCON in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Team THETA172"
    website: "https://github.com/shriomverma100/FALCON"
repository-code: "https://github.com/shriomverma100/FALCON"
url: "https://github.com/shriomverma100/FALCON"
abstract: >-
  FALCON discovers the cryptography an organisation depends on across source
  code, binaries, libraries, container images, certificates, keys, protocol
  configuration, live TLS endpoints and cloud key management. It measures the
  exposure of each finding to a cryptographically relevant quantum computer
  using Mosca's inequality, maps it to the NIST, NSA and EU transition
  deadlines, and recommends ML-KEM, ML-DSA or hybrid replacements benchmarked
  on the host. It produces a CycloneDX 1.6 cryptography bill of materials,
  SARIF, SPDX and CSV reports, and snapshots signed with ML-DSA-65 that third
  parties can verify. Built for Smart India Hackathon problem statement 26164
  (Enterprise Cryptographic Discovery and Analysis Tool), set by the National
  Technical Research Organisation.
keywords:
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - cryptographic inventory
  - CBOM
  - CycloneDX
  - Mosca's inequality
  - harvest now decrypt later
  - ML-KEM
  - ML-DSA
  - FIPS 203
  - FIPS 204
  - migration planning
  - SARIF
